        "license": "CCBYSA3.0; viewed only",
        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Entire1280x960 doorway picture inspected. Deep aligned open rectangular passages, carved round/pilaster jambs, thick lintels, multiple moulded stone courses, narrow stairs to raised thresholds. Exact relief narratives and individual block inventory omitted."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cambodia-2780_(3625344753).jpg",
        "author": "Dennis G. Jarvis",
        "date": "2009-02-04",
        "license": "CCBYSA2.0; viewed only",
        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Entire1280x850 exterior picture inspected. Rough warm laterite enclosure, broad lower courses, a tall sandstone-trimmed open portal with partially broken crest, low wall crown. Small sanctuary tip behind wall does not fully resolve its profile."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Banteay_samre_tower.JPG",
        "author": "Henry Flower",
        "date": "2010-11-07",
        "license": "CCBYSA3.0; viewed only",
        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Entire500x750 central-tower picture inspected to fill the prior cropped crown gap. Tall complete tapered lotus-bud/stacked miniature-storey crown, rounded upper termination, recessed miniature doors and corner projections, lower tall plain stone panels, triangular scrolling pediments and high moulded plinth. Roofed mandapa meets its side. Exact leaf/figure carvings are simplified."
      }
    ],
    "scope": "Specific mapped Banteay Samré: low laterite outer enclosure and four open gates; inner sandstone gallery with true open passages and window recesses; tall stepped lotus-bud sanctuary on a moulded plinth, eastern mandapa and two separately based libraries, corbelled roofs, original simplified pediment rims and stairs. Inner courts retain native ground. Heights, unmapped hall/library placement, surviving roof details and exact carving are picture-led approximations."
  }
